# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Allow-list deploy. NOTHING in this folder is published to GitHub Pages
# unless it is explicitly listed below. So any PDFs, reports, notes, or
# scratch files you keep here stay on your computer and never reach the
# public site — even ones you add later.
#
# To publish a new top-level file/folder, add another "!/name" line.
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# 1) Ignore everything at the project root by default
/*

# 2) ...then publish ONLY the web app:
!/.gitignore
!/.nojekyll
!/index.html
!/progress.html
!/exam.html
!/custom.html
!/README.md
!/shared/
!/Linear_Equations_App/
!/Linear_Functions_App/
!/Nonlinear_Functions_App/
!/Systems_and_Expressions_App_v2/
!/Proportionality_App/
!/Statistical_Reasoning_App/
!/Core_Geometry_App/
!/Analytical_Geometry_App/
!/Data_Analysis_Probability_App/
!/Challenge_App/

# OS cruft, even inside published folders
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# NOTE: this repo IS the public site (Pages serves the root), so anything
# tracked here is world-readable. Never allow-list a file holding a password,
# a key, or student data. Tutor-side tooling (build_challenge_set.py, the
# runbooks) is deliberately NOT published — it stays local.
